note right of computational_foundations
  TOPIC LEGEND

  computational_thinking:
  Computational thinking and algorithmic problem solving.

  programming_basics:
  Variables, expressions, statements, functions,
  conditionals, and iteration.

  computation_limits:
  Computational complexity, abstract machines,
  and undecidable problems.

  python_language:
  Python programming, names, visibility,
  mutable and immutable objects.

  program_control:
  Recursion, iteration, higher-order functions,
  exceptions, assertions, and interactive programs.

  python_software_tools:
  Python modules, packages, development environments,
  file operations, shell commands, testing, and debugging.

  data_structures:
  Data structures and abstract data types used in programs.

  algorithm_design:
  Sorting, dynamic programming, and sequence alignment algorithms.

  algorithm_analysis:
  Analysis of algorithmic procedures and computational complexity.

  computer_systems:
  Operating systems, computer networks, and information systems.

  architecture_hardware:
  Computer architecture, digital logic, chips, CPUs,
  memory, storage, input/output, and performance.

  operating_systems:
  Operating-system concepts, including Linux as a work environment.

  distributed_computing:
  Parallel computing, cloud computing, and big-data processing.

  object_oriented_design:
  Classes, objects, attributes, methods, and object-oriented computing.

  software_quality:
  Software production, program evaluation, testing, and debugging.

  software_modeling:
  UML for visualizing software application design.

  data_representation:
  Data types, tables, data models, JSON, CSV,
  web pages, and multimedia representations.

  data_wrangling:
  CSV processing, data cleaning, web scraping,
  and manipulation with Python data-analysis tools.

  data_visualization:
  Graphs as computational representations and visualization libraries.

  digital_productivity:
  Spreadsheets, word processing, image manipulation,
  graphics, and search engines as software tools.

  scientific_computing:
  Scientific computing with Python for analyzing,
  visualizing, and modeling scientific datasets,
  including numerical physical-equation models.

  statistical_computing:
  Statistical libraries, inference, probability distributions,
  confidence intervals, statistical tests, model analysis,
  and Monte Carlo simulation.

  data_analytics:
  Descriptive, diagnostic, predictive, and prescriptive
  analytics, including regression and classification.

  data_pipelines:
  Data acquisition through analysis and valorization.

  domain_data:
  Biological data types and structures, plus financial
  problems and access to financial data.

  machine_learning:
  Supervised and unsupervised machine-learning algorithms
  and models used in data-science applications.

  deep_learning_ai:
  Neural networks, convolutional, recurrent, and LSTM networks,
  GANs, autoencoders, transformers, and machine-learning frameworks.

  language_ai:
  Natural-language processing, topic modeling,
  and large language models.
end note

